Divine energy is the stuff a god is made of. It cannot be created and cannot be destroyed; when a divine being dies its energy leaks out into the surroundings and spreads, the way heat leaves a room. Passed down a line of descendants it only dilutes, which is how the [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessians]] thin and lose it. It works differently from mortal energy, the kind a mortal caster draws on.

[[Geography/Althane/index|Althane]] is unusually rich in it because three gods have bled into the ground there for hundreds of thousands of years, and it can be mined from the soil. A place cut off from the outside world holds what divine energy is released inside it, so a thing killed in a closed room leaves its power there to be gathered up. [[People/Althane/Henrik|Henrik]]'s [[Phenomena/Althane/Divine Amphora|Divine Amphora]] moves it from one vessel to another.

The [[Divinity/Althane/The Stranger|Stranger]] is the reverse of a Thessian: he began mortal and burns mortal energy, so he needs others to turn the divine energy of Althane into mortal energy for him.
